WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.261
- [Narrator] So you think
Tinder is a recent phenomenon.

00:00:03.261 --> 00:00:05.720
What if I told you Tinder on paper

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.440
existed back in the Victorian days?

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.190
Here's what happened.

00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:15.713
Way before Hallmark, people
used personal calling cards

00:00:15.713 --> 00:00:17.633
to connect with each other.

00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:19.195
Picture this.

00:00:19.195 --> 00:00:20.374
It was the late 1800s.

00:00:20.374 --> 00:00:22.555
A man and a woman crossed paths.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.617
They exchange a look.

00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:25.654
In return, the man passed his card.

00:00:25.654 --> 00:00:29.071
See, society at that time was very formal

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:33.057
and not satisfied with the
stiff social conventions,

00:00:33.057 --> 00:00:35.137
youngsters got creative.

00:00:35.137 --> 00:00:39.355
Enter escort cards, the
calling card with a twist.

00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:42.177
Think of the most ridiculous
and cheesy pickup line

00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:44.635
you've ever heard written on a card.

00:00:44.635 --> 00:00:46.151
- [Man] Come and see our new lamp.

00:00:46.151 --> 00:00:48.395
You can turn it down so
low that there is scarcely

00:00:48.395 --> 00:00:51.652
any light at all, P.S.
our sofa just holds two.

00:00:51.652 --> 00:00:53.915
- [Man] I'm just your size and complexion,

00:00:53.915 --> 00:00:56.294
I'm going in your direction,
so if you have no objection,

00:00:56.294 --> 00:00:58.950
I'd like to be your protection.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:03.073
- [Man] I am C.Y. Young,
who the devil are you?.

00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:05.351
- [Narrator] Now, picture
that card slipped to you,

00:01:05.351 --> 00:01:07.137
it was a way to flirt in public

00:01:07.137 --> 00:01:08.737
without anyone ever knowing.

00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:10.715
- [Man] May I have the pleasure

00:01:10.715 --> 00:01:11.873
of seeing you home this evening?

00:01:11.873 --> 00:01:14.593
- [Narrator] And in this
case, oh, she swiped left.

00:01:14.593 --> 00:01:15.812
Sorry.

00:01:15.812 --> 00:01:18.812
(soft violin music)

